# ============================================================================
# Multi-opening-item blink fix (2026-07-18, precise user repro)
#
# ROOT CAUSE (from user report: undoing the 3rd door blinks doors 1&2, windows
# don't; different types never cross-blink): consecutive same-type openings drawn
# in one session are multiple POINTS in a single OpeningController item. On point-
# count decrease, OpeningController.Rebuild called transform.ClearChildren() — nuking
# and recreating EVERY opening instance in that item → the survivors blink. AND the
# undo reconciler recreated the whole opening item (delete+add) on any point change,
# which also destroyed all its instances.
#
# FloorMapDesigner/Scripts/Controllers/OpeningController.cs: Rebuild removes ONLY the
#   excess trailing children (detach + DestroyUniversal), keeping/reusing the rest.
# IBMROSBridge/UndoRedo/RestoreReconciler.cs: SetItemPointsInPlace (generalizes
#   MovePointsInPlace to add/remove control points) — reconcile an item's points IN
#   PLACE for BOTH rooms and openings, keeping the item (and its surviving opening
#   instances) alive. Reconciler geometry-diff no longer delete+adds openings.
#   + Debug.Log diagnostics ([IBMROS Reconcile] scoped:.. / full-restore: reason).
#   + type-morph now recreates just that item (was full-restore fallback).
# ApiSmokeTest.cs step 15: 3-point door -> 2, surviving opening GameObject instances
#   preserved (no blink).
#
# Note (obs 3, minor): adding openings very fast coalesces into one undo step (they
# fall within the 0.4s capture settle window) -> undo removes them together. Logged
# as finer-undo-granularity future work, not fixed now.
# ============================================================================

