# REVERT in-place opening reconcile (2026-07-18) — corruption regression
#
# The in-place point reconcile for multi-point OPENING items (added earlier same day
# to kill the item-blink) caused worse problems in interactive stress testing
# (10+ doors): doors desynced from their wall holes, doors shifted, the building
# vanished/needed redo. Root: reconciling a multi-point OpeningController's points in
# place during undo chains desyncs the parametric wall holes from the door visuals and
# can leave bad state. Reverted: RestoreReconciler geometry-diff recreates the changed
# OPENING item (delete+add, correct load path, scoped to that item + its room); ROOMS
# still reconcile in place. Correctness > the item-blink. OpeningController remove-excess
# fix + SetItemPointsInPlace method + diagnostics kept (correct in isolation, tested).
# Blink of the CHANGED opening item returns (acceptable); proper blink-free opening undo
# needs interactive diagnostics + verification (see [IBMROS Reconcile] console logs).
# Separate open issue: rapid opening adds coalesce into one undo step (0.4s settle
# window) -> multiple removed per undo. Undo-granularity redesign, not yet done.
