# ============================================================================
# One-opening-per-item (2026-07-18, user-chosen proper fix for opening undo blink)
#
# Root of the blink: consecutive same-type openings drawn in one session were POINTS
# in ONE OpeningController item, so undo recreated the whole item -> survivors blink.
# The gateway (AddOpening) already makes one item per opening; this makes the
# INTERACTIVE draw loop do the same.
#
# ControlPointsController.cs: + public singlePointMode. On placing a ghost point in
#   singlePointMode: stop drawing this item (IsDrawing=false) and call
#   UIFloorMapMenu.ContinueDrawingNewOpening(this).
# OpeningController.cs: Init sets cpc.singlePointMode = true (rooms stay multi-point).
# UIFloorMapMenu.cs: + ContinueDrawingNewOpening(cpc) arms a fresh opening of the same
#   type; DisableDrawModeOnItems(disableAll) -> RemoveEmptyOpenings (delete the trailing
#   0-point armed opening); GetItemsData skips 0-point openings (clean snapshots/saves).
#
# Result: each door/window is its own item -> undo removes one at a time with NO blink
# of others (proven by the gateway-based apitest, which already uses one-item-per-opening
# and verifies scoped/clean undo), and openings become independently selectable/deletable.
# NEEDS interactive verification (draw-loop timing) — headless tests can't drive taps.
# ============================================================================
